menu "My UPS Pal Tailscale"

config UPSA_TAILSCALE
    bool "Tailscale on the board"
    depends on UPSA_BOARD_REV_B && SPIRAM
    default n
    help
        Joins this board to a tailnet with MicroLink (components/microlink),
        so NUT on 3493 and the web UI are reachable from anywhere on the
        tailnet without a subnet router. Rev B only: MicroLink keeps half a
        megabyte or more of control-plane state in PSRAM, which the N4 does
        not have.

        This only builds the client in. Whether it runs, and with which auth
        key, is set on the board from the web UI and kept in NVS -- never in
        the image, which is published for every board to download.

        Build it with sdkconfig.defaults.tailscale layered after
        sdkconfig.defaults.revb; that file sets the mbedTLS and lwIP options
        MicroLink needs. See components/tailnet/README.md.

endmenu
